# Citation metadata for this repository.
# Multi-paper collection: GitHub reads only the ROOT CITATION.cff for its
# "Cite this repository" button, so this file cites paper #1 (The Prime
# Staircase), the repository's founding paper. Per-paper BibTeX lives in
# each paper's folder README. To make the button cite a different paper,
# edit title/keywords/url/abstract below.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "The Prime Staircase: Superexponential Growth along the Diagonal of the Hierarchy of Higher-Order Primes"
authors:
  - family-names: Tapiador
    given-names: Justo
    affiliation: Universidad de Alicante
type: unpublished
year: 2026
keywords:
  - prime numbers
  - prime-indexed primes
  - higher-order primes
  - primeth recurrence
  - asymptotic growth
  - OEIS
repository: "https://github.com/Justo-Tapiador/maths"
url: "https://github.com/Justo-Tapiador/maths/blob/main/prime-staircase/prime_staircase.pdf"
abstract: "Study of the diagonal d_k = f^(k+1)(k) of the hierarchy of
  higher-order primes: a master formula for its growth, log d_k ~ k log k ~ p_k,
  structural theorems (order-of-primeness ladder, orbit crossings), exact
  computation of d_1..d_10 and rigorous brackets for d_11..d_14."
